        <item>
            <title>1.0.16</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 15:48:10 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>163</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.16</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font: -apple-system-body, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  ul { margin: 6px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  p { margin: 6px 0; }
</style>
<ul>
<li>Fans speed up quickly when the temperature rises, but slow down more gently afterwards. In Sensor mode, and after an Auto-Blast trip, they now take around twice as long to come back down, so they no longer drop straight to a lower speed the moment a spike passes.</li>
<li>The CPU and GPU graphs turn from blue to amber and then red as the temperature climbs, and show the highest and average temperature for the last five minutes. Normal temperatures are blue everywhere, to match the graphs.</li>
<li>The window&#x27;s title bar takes the page&#x27;s colour, so scrolled content hides under it cleanly.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
